# Walkthrough - Resolve `@/lib/utils` Import Error

I have successfully resolved the issue where the `@/lib/utils` module could not be found.

## Root Cause

The error "Cannot find module '@/lib/utils' or its corresponding type declarations" occurred because the [tsconfig.json](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/tsconfig.json) was missing the `baseUrl` property. Even though `paths` was defined, TypeScript needs a `baseUrl` to know from which directory it should start resolving those paths.

## Changes Made

### Configuration

#### [MODIFY] [tsconfig.json](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/tsconfig.json)

- Added `"baseUrl": "."` to the `compilerOptions`.

## Verification Results

### Automated Tests
- I ran `npx tsc --noEmit` which now passes without any errors related to `@/lib/utils`.
- I verified that the required dependencies (`clsx` and `tailwind-merge`) are correctly installed.

```bash
$ npm list clsx tailwind-merge
backend-proyecto@1.0.0 /Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto informatico_1 frontend/Proyecto_Informatico
├── clsx@2.1.1
└── tailwind-merge@3.5.0
```

### Visual Check
- The [GlassCard.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/proyecto%20informatico_1%20frontend/Proyecto_Informatico/src/components/ui/GlassCard.tsx) file should no longer show any import errors in your IDE.
